Use _mm256_cvtph_ps on clang for AVX-F16C half-to-float in skcms.

GCC exposes __builtin_ia32_vcvtph2ps256 as a built-in; clang does not.
Clang only provides the F16C half-to-float conversion through the
portable intrinsic name _mm256_cvtph_ps (which it implements via
__builtin_convertvector, not the ia32 built-in). Calling the raw GCC
built-in unconditionally therefore breaks the clang build with:

  error: use of undeclared identifier '__builtin_ia32_vcvtph2ps256'

Both compilers implement _mm256_cvtph_ps, so route clang through the
portable name while leaving the GCC path untouched. The reverse
direction (__builtin_ia32_vcvtps2ph256, line 191) is present in clang
and needs no change.

--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/Transform_inl.h
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/Transform_inl.h
@@ -161,8 +161,12 @@ SI F F_from_Half(U16 half) {
 #elif defined(USING_AVX512F)
     return (F)_mm512_cvtph_ps((__m256i)half);
 #elif defined(USING_AVX_F16C)
+#if defined(__clang__)
+    return (F)_mm256_cvtph_ps((__m128i)half);
+#else
     typedef int16_t __attribute__((vector_size(16))) I16;
     return __builtin_ia32_vcvtph2ps256((I16)half);
+#endif
 #else
     U32 wide = cast<U32>(half);
     // A half is 1-5-10 sign-exponent-mantissa, with 15 exponent bias.
